# Prompt: Khushdil Ayurvedic Clinic, 3D scroll website

## What it is

Build a single-file website for Khushdil Ayurvedic Clinic, run by Vaid Dr. Jashan Sandhu. Use plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript. No framework, no build step, no libraries. It is a warm paper-coloured page with deep forest green, antique gold and turmeric accents. It reads like a printed apothecary catalogue that comes alive in 3D.

One page, six scroll chapters:
1. Hero: headline over a curved, endlessly drifting row of video cards (his Instagram reels).
2. The Dispensary: an endless shelf of herbal medicine boxes, spine out. One box is pulled out and physically turned in 3D to show its front. Clicking it opens a detail sheet.
3. The Journey: a pinned scroll story where five glass plates fly past in 3D, one per step.
4. The Vaid: portrait, story, and an endless ingredient marquee.
5. Patient Stories: a 3D tilted card carousel.
6. Book: a form that opens WhatsApp with the answers prefilled.

Everything is driven by one requestAnimationFrame loop plus the Web Animations API. No CSS keyframes. There is NO opacity fade anywhere: every reveal is a mask slide, a clip or a scale.

## Content rules (important)

- Real facts (use exactly): clinic name Khushdil Ayurvedic Clinic; doctor Dr. Jashan Sandhu (Vaid); Instagram @vaid.jashansandhu (https://www.instagram.com/vaid.jashansandhu), 13K+ followers; phones 62846-64722 and 78889-49756 (India, +91); bio lines "Ayurvedic: Balance Life Naturally", "Old Generation Business", "Only Ayurvedic Medicine".
- Placeholders, shown in square brackets and easy to find in one DATA object: degree, years of experience, clinic address, city, timings, reviews, the treatment list, and every treatment description. The doctor must confirm all of these.
- Never write "99.9% result", "100% cure", "guaranteed", or any promise of curing a named disease. Use soft words: "support", "care", "guidance". Footer disclaimer is required.
- Never invent reviews or numbers. Review cards show "[Real review here]" until real ones are pasted.

