### Curved reel carousel
Ten tall cards scroll right to left at 50u per second, looping seamlessly, pitch 196u. Pointer and touch drag follows 1:1, coasts after release (velocity decays about 95% per second), then auto-scroll resumes. Cursor grab / grabbing. Drive the scroll from a long WAAPI clock (document.documentElement.animate(..., {duration: 1e9})) so it is time-based.
- Curve: for a card, t is its unpushed offset from x = 720. Centre x = 720 + t*(1 + 0.083*(t/706)^2). Normalised distance d = |x - 720| / 706.
- Width = (170 + 48*d^2)u. Each vertical edge's height = (280 + 92*q^2.6)u, where q is that edge's own normalised distance. Vertical centre = (604 - 12*d^2)u.
- Result: centre cards are upright 170x280; edge cards grow to about 370u tall and lean like the inside of a cylinder.
- Draw each card as a rounded quad with clip-path: path(), 15u corners, recomputed each frame. No drop shadow. A small frosted round play icon bottom-left. Cards are clipped by the frame edge.
- Each card holds a <video> (ASSET.reels[i], muted, loop, playsinline, preload metadata) over its poster, cover-fitted. Only play cards that are on screen. Click opens the Instagram profile in a new tab.

### Entrance (one-time WAAPI sequence)
